-- EXPECT-ERROR: Only public functions of
-- Slice 6 (proof caps), the mint_cap PRIVATE-FN witness -- the minting surface
-- is exactly the PUBLIC (`fn`) functions of the declaring module; a `pfn`
-- (private function) of the declaring module is NOT a mint surface (it may
-- pass a proof cap through, like any external code, but may not construct
-- one). Here `Db`'s own `pfn run_migrations` tries to `mint_cap` its own
-- `Cap(Db.Migrated)`; Check 6's private-in-declaring-module branch rejects it
-- with `` private function `run_migrations` in `Db` cannot mint
-- `Cap(Db.Migrated)`. Only public functions of `Db` can construct
-- `Cap(Db.Migrated)`. ``. Making the fn public (`fn`) is exactly the accept
-- case (`accept/t62`). IMPOSSIBLE to reject pre-fix (`mint_cap` is new to this
-- slice). See core-march-types.md §2.8.13.
mod Db do
  proof cap Migrated
  needs IO

  pfn run_migrations(cap : Cap(IO)) : Cap(Db.Migrated) do
    mint_cap(cap)
  end
end
